# Fork-owned SSoT trio (see docs/designs/t3-company-os-ssot.md): prefer OUR
# side when a selective upstream cherry-pick/merge touches these files.
# Convenience, not a guarantee — the driver must be defined once per clone
# (`git config merge.ours.driver true`; .gitattributes alone cannot ship it)
# and it only fires on both-sides-changed merges. The real protection is
# `pnpm check:ssot-guards` (scripts/check-ssot-guards.mjs) in CI.
/roadmap.md merge=ours
/backlog.md merge=ours
/design.md merge=ours
